 "answer": "The function is **`load_index_from_storage`**, imported from `llama_index.core`. You pass it a `StorageContext`, usually one created from the persist directory:\n\n```python\nfrom llama_index.core import StorageContext, load_index_from_storage\n\nstorage_context = StorageContext.from_defaults(persist_dir=\"./storage\")\nindex = load_index_from_storage(storage_context)\n```\n\nTo load a specific index when the storage directory holds several, pass its ID with `index_id=\"...\"`. I'm confident in this for recent LlamaIndex versions, but I can't check the exact signature against your installed version.",
